&lt;/ul></description></item><item><title>ssh</title><link>https://chacin.dev/notes/ssh/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://chacin.dev/notes/ssh/</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="section-header" id="forward-traffic-through-an-ssh-server">
 &lt;a class="section-header" href="#forward-traffic-through-an-ssh-server">Forward Traffic through an SSH server&lt;/a>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>The command below creates a SOCKS server which can be used as
a proxy to forward traffic through a host.&lt;/p>








&lt;div class="code-block">
 &lt;div class="code-block-tabs">
 
 
 &lt;div class="code-block-lang">
 &lt;p>sh&lt;/p>
 &lt;/div>
 
 
 
 &lt;/div>
 &lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">ssh -d &lt;span class="m">8080&lt;/span> &amp;lt;user&amp;gt;@&amp;lt;server&amp;gt;&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;p>Once ready, you can open your browser and set it to use your
proxy server. Below is what the option looks like for Firefox.&lt;/p>
&lt;p class="center">&lt;img src="https://chacin.dev/notes/ssh/images/firefox_proxy_setting.png" alt="Menu in Firefox for configuring proxy settings"
